<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Küçük Kaynarca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1774</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1768-1774">Russo-Turkish War (1768–1774)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Küçük Kaynarca was signed in 1774 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1768-1774">Russo-Turkish War</a> of 1768–1774. It made the Crimean Khanate independent of the Ottomans and gave Russia a foothold on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. It also granted Russia a claimed right to intervene on behalf of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christian subjects.</p></div>
